Description: antinomie: hash the files a run writes at their last close, and the launched program's image, on request
Author: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Origin: project
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-21

The tracer hashed an executed image and a file about to be deleted, but not what a run leaves behind in the files it writes, and not the launched program itself: the kernel starts it without a traced execve, so its exec had no call to hang a hash on.  A run launched with the new EXEC flag HASH_WRITES gets a SHA-256 of each regular file one of its tasks had open for writing, when the file's last writer lets it go (the inode's writer count drops to zero in __fput()): after close() in task work, at exit, or after the call that dropped the last reference. A memfd, which has no write access to count, is the same when its last reference goes. The job takes the same path as the others: references and a small job in the closing task, never a sleep or a wait; the read on the system unbound workqueue with a private no-notify, no-atime open; the same 16 MiB file limit, 16 queued jobs and 64 MiB queued; the same refusal records and the same CHANGED comparison, against the file as the last close left it. Pseudo filesystems (proc, sysfs, cgroup and the like) and files that are not regular publish nothing. A refusal decided outside a traced call is published by the worker too, under the identity taken at the close.  The record (kind WRITE, layout antinomie.hash/2, 112 bytes) is the hash/1 record followed by the file's device, inode, generation, mode and link count at the close, because the call it belongs to, the closing task's last, need not name the file. A task that has left its run at exit still finds the run by its root cookie.  With EXEC flag HASH_ROOT the launched program's own image is hashed at its exec commit, as an EXEC record under the launch's identity (call id 0, the "lifecycle.launch" event's).  The new optional command TRACER_CAPS lists the optional EXEC flags a guest accepts and its hashing budget; an older guest answers -EOPNOTSUPP and must not be sent the flags, which it would reject. A host that does not know them sends neither flag and sees nothing new. The contract revision stays 17.

